/HAFiscal-candidate.pdf
/HAFiscal-candidate.dep
/Appendix-HANK.dep
/Subfiles/*.dep

# HOT-mode scratch (Code/HA-Models/hot_mode.py, 2026-09-07): a hot run's Step-5 outputs are
# suffixed `_hot`, its Step-2 calibration goes to .hot_results_out/, its policy/equilibrium
# store to .hot_policy_store/, and the paper exhibits it would otherwise touch are held in
# .hot_exhibit_snapshot/ for the duration. None of it is a result; none of it is tracked.
Code/HA-Models/.hot_exhibit_snapshot/
Code/HA-Models/.hot_results_out/
Code/HA-Models/.hot_policy_store/
Code/HA-Models/FromPandemicCode/Tables/*_hot/
Code/HA-Models/FromPandemicCode/Figures/*_hot/
# HOT regression check: every run is captured under hot_runs/, and the blessed reference is
# hot_reference/. BOTH are per-machine local state, like the policy store, and neither is
# tracked: the check answers "did this session break the mainline on THIS machine", byte
# identity across machines is not expected (the recorded cross-platform wobble), and the
# global `*_candidate.*` / `*.csv` ignores would drop exactly the numeric products from any
# tracked subset. Bless on the known-good tree at the start of a session; check at the end.
Code/HA-Models/hot_runs/
Code/HA-Models/hot_reference/
# Welfare-band pairing (2026-09-07): the blessed per-world reference band for the seed-paired
# C4 gate is per-machine local state like hot_reference/ (make welfare-reference / welfare-check).
Code/HA-Models/welfare_reference/
